mibpkg web interfacemibsdk-dev <p>Open mibpkg from your phone, upload the <code>.mpk</code>, review the permissions and approve. mibpkg writes the jar, the icons and the grants, then asks the running SDK to load the plugin. No HMI restart is needed.</p> <pre><code>installer/mibsdk-dev install-plugin build/mibsdk/coffee-timer-1.0.0.mpk &lt;unit-ip&gt;
# exit 3 lists the permissions; re-run with:
installer/mibsdk-dev install-plugin build/mibsdk/coffee-timer-1.0.0.mpk \
    --approve=ui.slot.carmenu,ui.slot.statusbar &lt;unit-ip&gt;
</code></pre> <p><code>mibsdk-dev</code> reads the unit address from the last argument or <code>MIBSDK_HOST</code>.</p>

mibpkg web interfacemibpkg on the unitmibsdk-dev over SSH <p>Open mibpkg's web interface from your phone (the address is shown in GEM → mibpkg), upload the <code>.mpk</code> and install it. mibpkg lists the permissions in plain words and asks you to approve them.</p> <pre><code>mibpkg install-file mibsdk &lt;upload-id&gt; - --approve=...
</code></pre> <p><code>mibpkg</code> exits with status 3 and lists the permissions until you re-run it with the approval. The exact upload flow is described in the mibpkg README.</p> <pre><code>installer/mibsdk-dev install &lt;unit-ip&gt;
</code></pre> <p><code>mibsdk-dev</code> uploads <code>dist/build/dist/mibsdk-*.mpk</code>, runs mibpkg and passes its exit status through. Use <code>MIBSDK_HOST</code> instead of the last argument if you prefer.</p>
